From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:08:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Rotate misfit tasks with tasks on busy bigger
 CPUs

Load balancing moves a misfit task to a bigger CPU only when the bigger
CPU's group has spare capacity (update_sd_pick_busiest() rejects a misfit
source when the local group is not group_has_spare). When every bigger
CPU already runs one task, nothing moves: the task that started on a
small CPU keeps it for as long as the others run. Equal tasks then make
unequal progress, and work split evenly across all CPUs ends with a tail
in which the tasks that started on small CPUs finish alone on big ones.

On the M4 Pro (T6040, 10 P cores at capacity 1024 and 4 E cores at 383)
a 14-thread CoreMark runs for about 15 s with all CPUs busy, then the 4
threads that ran on the E cores finish alone on P cores about 5 s later.
It scores 425k iter/s against 546k on macOS on the same machine. Rotating
the benchmark's threads across all CPUs every 20 ms from user space gives
545k, so the loss is all placement.

Once a task has been misfit on a CPU for four base slices, have the tick
queue a work item that swaps it with the task on a busy bigger CPU,
using migrate_swap(). Bigger CPUs are taken round robin, so each task on
them takes its turn on a smaller CPU and the big CPUs are time shared
the way one runqueue would share them. The swap only happens when every
allowed bigger CPU runs exactly one fair task, since an idle one pulls
the misfit task through the existing misfit balancing, and it never
moves down a task with a higher weight or a higher uclamp_min than the
misfit task. Kernel threads and pinned tasks are left alone.

migrate_swap() was built only for NUMA balancing; build it on every SMP
kernel, and keep the NUMA tracepoint for the NUMA caller.

The MISFIT_ROTATE scheduler feature is on by default, like the other
fair class heuristics.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 2d24fbce39a391c5e450deda3793b71d7aa25ea2)
---
